ance. Otherwise it’s discrimination, just like it would be if you refused a young worker because “younger people are less reliable”—even if that matched your personal observation. So, I’m not denying you’ve seen a pattern. But patterns aren’t rules, and acting on them as if they are carries real risk. The safest, most respectful path remains: set out the overtime, ask who wants it, hand it out fairly from the volunteers. Nature will take its course—if the over-sixties never volunteer, you’ll get the result you expected. But if one does step forward, you might be pleasantly surprised.
